# /usr/bin/tempio is a pre-compiled Go binary bundled inside
# ghcr.io/home-assistant/base-python by the Home Assistant team.
# These CVEs are in that upstream binary's stdlib/x/crypto and cannot
# be fixed by this project — they require a base-image update from HA.
# Track: https://github.com/home-assistant/docker-base
#
# Re-verified 2026-08-07 against the current :latest base image (amd64,
# index digest sha256:ba50cdf…). Both entries are still load-bearing — pulling
# usr/bin/tempio out of the image and reading its embedded build info gives:
#
#   tempio: go1.23.3
#     dep golang.org/x/crypto v0.26.0
#     -ldflags "-X main.TempioVersion=2024.11.2"   vcs.time 2024-11-26
#
# CVE-2024-45337 is fixed in x/crypto 0.31.0 (shipping 0.26.0), and
# CVE-2025-68121 is fixed in Go 1.24.13 / 1.25.7 (built with 1.23.3), so the
# base image still carries both. HA has not rebuilt tempio since 2024-11-26.
#
# To re-check without a Docker daemon: pull the amd64 manifest from
# ghcr.io/v2/home-assistant/base-python, download the layer blobs, untar
# usr/bin/tempio, then `go version -m tempio`. Drop whichever entry the
# reported x/crypto and Go versions have moved past.
CVE-2024-45337
CVE-2025-68121
